{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_pc_02_draft_intercombination_lines", "label": "Intercombination lines: 576 E1 cells with Delta S != 0", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PC-02-draft.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Whether the 576 lines are forbidden or allowed is a property of the coupling scheme and not of the atom: LS forbids them, jK does not, and the same transitions are present or absent according to which scheme names them."}, {"id": "recovered_pc_02_draft_ls_spin_selection_rule", "label": "LS spin selection rule Delta S = 0 and its spin-orbit breakdown", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PC-02-draft.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rule is not exact in nature: spin-orbit interaction mixes states of different S and the mixing grows with nuclear charge, so intercombination lines strengthen down a group and are ordinary in heavy atoms."}, {"id": "recovered_pc_02_draft_jk_coupling_index", "label": "Lambda_9 is built in jK coupling, not LS", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PC-02-draft.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A jK-built index couples each electron's orbital and spin before combining, so S is not a good quantum number of the scheme and Delta S = 0 is not one of its rules; imposing the spin rule anyway keeps 526 cells at E = 0."}, {"id": "recovered_pc_02_draft_russell_saunders", "label": "Russell & Saunders 1925", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "recovered/PC-02-draft.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_pc_02_draft_intercombination_lines", "target": "recovered_pc_02_draft_ls_spin_selection_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": 